Risk and Control – Rimas
Rimas has made some very good contributions to strengthening security controls across our Container Security portfolio. 
His original work on image-age validation has become an important part of our VSaaS Gating controls in LSE, helping ensure teams use images that meet our defined age requirements.
Another achievement was his contribution of the Operator Pipeline integration into 3PiiP. He helped move the old process away from a manual and error-prone approach to a controlled ingestion process, where Operator images go through 3PiiP validation before being brought into Citi. This has strengthened our security controls and improved consistency in how operator third-party images are ingested.
I also value Rimas's involvement in reviewing other developers' PRs. He provides direct and constructive feedback, often on time-sensitive changes, helping maintain code quality and engineering standards across our Container Security codebase. I consider this a high-impact contribution, as it provides an important human control within our engineering process, helping ensure code quality, security and engineering excellence before changes are released into production.
One good example was the VSaaS Gating implementation, where the initial PR was particularly large. Rimas provided some good feedback that helped break the changes into smaller, more manageable PRs, making them easier to review, validate and maintain. This demonstrates his attention to engineering quality and his willingness to help other developers deliver better solutions.
I would encourage him to continue sharing his technical knowledge and maintaining the high standard of his PR reviews. Going forward, I would also like him to focus on creating more opportunities for other team members to get involved and contribute to workstreams such as the Operator Pipeline and CHRIS. This includes ensuring knowledge is shared effectively across the team and making it easier for others to contribute independently. This will help build wider team capability, develop other engineers' skills and strengthen the team's overall ownership of these workstreams.

